# Rules for agents working in this repo with a small local model (Qwen via Cline)

## Read order at session start
0. **Сначала выполни `node tools/project-status.mjs`** — это факты с диска: коммит,
   сколько форм в каталоге и в мире, подключён ли каталог, какие файлы T03 существуют,
   статусы бэклога. Документы могут отставать, вывод этой команды — нет.
1. `.planning/STATE.md` — current task and what is actually done. Read first, update last.
2. The task file it points to, under `.planning/tasks/`.
3. `.planning/CONCEPT.md` — the design source of truth. Read only what your task needs.
Ready-to-paste prompts for the current task live in `.planning/prompts-T03.md`.

## How to work
- Work in small steps. One tool call per message.
- Never read more files than the current task names. Never read node_modules, .git, or build output.
- If a fact is not in the files you were told to read, say you don't know and stop.
  Do not guess file names, function names, or paths.
- Do not touch files the task did not name. Do not reformat code you were not asked to change.
- When the task says STOP, stop and report: what you changed, what command you ran, and its exact output.
- On Windows use `cd /d` when changing drives, or pass absolute paths instead of relying on cd.
- **One task per session.** Finish one `T##`, update bookkeeping, commit, then STOP.
  Do not start the next task in the same session.
- **В конце сессии обнови `.planning/STATE.md`**: строку текущей задачи и запись в журнал
  сессий (что сделано, чем проверено, что осталось). Без этого следующая сессия начнёт с
  неверной картины — так уже терялось время.
- End-of-session bookkeeping, in this order: task file status → `.planning/BACKLOG.md`
  → `.planning/STATE.md` (append a session-log row) → knowledge-graph files if behavior changed.
- Commit message format: `T##: <imperative summary>`.

## What this project is (concept v2, adopted 2026-08-20)

NEUROGLYPHS is an endless generative kaleidoscope explorer. You fly through infinite
abstract 3D worlds made entirely of glyphs, formulas and light. Each world is generated
deterministically from a seed; collected "things" fold back into the seed and shape the
next world. Music is the heartbeat — everything pulses and reacts to it. No goal, no
victory, no death. Every world has exactly ONE rectangular exit with a shaped hole.

Pillars: seed = world; music = heartbeat; no goal / no death; everything is symbols;
worlds are collectible (100 curated + infinite random + share by code); one exit.

**Concept v1 is dead.** If you find text about collecting tokens into a bounded context
window, inference events, synapses, neural-network layers, or the folders `src/systems/`,
`src/ui/`, `src/data/` — that is stale wording, not a requirement. Delete it instead of
implementing it. The last code leftover (`buildContextRing` in `src/main.js`) was renamed
to `buildOrbitRing` on 2026-08-21; the dead CSS rules `#context-bar`/`#context-fill`
were removed from `index.html` in the same session.

## Invariants
- INV-1: no `Math.random()` in world generation — seeded PRNG only (`src/core/rng.js`).
- INV-2: all visuals are glyph-based.
- INV-3: same seed = same world.
- INV-4: no player death, no fail state.
- INV-5: music drives pulsation and reactivity.
- INV-6: the exit is always rectangular and always findable.
- INV-8: no text inside the world; textual feedback belongs to the DOM HUD.

## Facts that are easy to get wrong
- The seed engine is `src/core/seed.js`, the PRNG is `src/core/rng.js`. There is no `src/data/`.
- There is **no bundler and no dependencies**. Three.js r160 arrives through a CDN import map
  in `index.html`. `npm run dev` (= `npm start`) serves static files via `server.js`;
  `npm run build` is deliberately a no-op.
- `npm test` runs plain node files and must print `DETERMINISM_OK` and `SEED_OK`
  (plus `WORLD_OK` once T03 lands).
- **Node tests cannot import `three`** — the import map only exists in the browser.
  Keep pure math (positions, counts, params) in separate exported functions and test those.
- Glyph textures: dispose them on rebuild, or GPU memory leaks.
- Commit messages and task files in English; docs and in-game text may be Russian.

## Recurring mistakes (add to this list when they repeat)
- **Seed round-trip:** concatenating per-field base36 chars gives ambiguous boundaries.
  Pack all fields into one integer (shift + OR), then convert to base36 once.
  Test the round-trip on ≥200 random parameter sets.
- **Export mismatch between module and test:** define the expected return shape in the task
  file before implementing, or write the test first.
- **Signature drift:** `randomSeed(rng?)` takes an optional argument, unlike what an older
  task file claimed. Record actual signatures in the task file.
- **Stale docs sending agents the wrong way:** an agent read the v1 concept and started
  designing a context-window mechanic that no longer exists. When a doc disagrees with
  `.planning/STATE.md`, STATE.md and CONCEPT.md win — and fix the stale doc separately.
- **`cd` in the terminal not taking effect:** an agent ran `git status` from the wrong
  directory and concluded the repo was corrupted. Use `cd /d` or absolute paths.

## Environment
- Windows 11, cmd shell, git available, `gh` CLI not installed.
- No `gh` auth: for pushing, use a token in the remote URL or ask the user. Never commit tokens.
